<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates softer to steady.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates softer to steady.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Short term Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were weaker while the one-year maturities remained unchanged, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders said the drop in overnight rates prompted banks to lower their swap rates, although some banks were still cautious in their long term outlook.</p>
<p>Short-term rates for the peso slid on Thursday after three days of rise as cash-strapped banks sold dollars to shore up liquidity, traders said.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 Dec 12		  Dec 11</p>
<p>    1 W		11  1/8		 11 5/16</p>
<p>    2 W		11 3/16		 11 3/16</p>
<p>    1 M		11 1/8		  11 1/4</p>
<p>    2 M		11  3/4		 11 3/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  3/16		11 1/4</p>
<p>    6 M		11  5/16		11 3/8</p>
<p>    12M		11 11/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    VALUE	    13 Dec		  12 Dec</p>
